2026-10-09T17:56:43.6435608Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6446173Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6446936Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6447412Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6447705Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6448005Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6448399Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6448857Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6449348Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6449553Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6449668Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6449953Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6450132Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6450338Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T17:56:43.6450688Z   $ sh ./install-nix
